{"seq":1,"slug":"pricing-foundations","title":"定价理论基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/quantitative-finance/derivatives-pricing/pricing-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"no-arbitrage-principle","title":"无套利原理与风险中性定价","url":"/l-doc-books/h/quantitative-finance/derivatives-pricing/pricing-foundations/no-arbitrage-principle","wordCount":2422,"readingTime":10},{"seq":2,"slug":"stochastic-calculus","title":"随机微积分基础：布朗运动与伊藤引理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/quantitative-finance/derivatives-pricing/pricing-foundations/stochastic-calculus","wordCount":2485,"readingTime":10},{"seq":3,"slug":"black-scholes-model","title":"Black-Scholes 模型与解析解","url":"/l-doc-books/h/quantitative-finance/derivatives-pricing/pricing-foundations/black-scholes-model","wordCount":2271,"readingTime":10}],"introMarkdown":"# 定价理论基础\n\n本章构建衍生品定价的数学根基。首先阐述无套利原理与风险中性定价的核心思想——这是整个衍生品定价理论的逻辑起点；然后系统介绍随机微积分的关键工具，包括布朗运动、伊藤积分与伊藤引理；最后推导 Black-Scholes 模型及其解析解，展示从随机过程假设到封闭形式定价公式的完整路径。三篇文档由浅入深，构成从金融直觉到数学严谨的完整链条。\n"}